                  <provenance type="#i" cert="low"><orgName role="fmo" key="org_622">Grimsby,
                        Lincolnshire. Austin Friars</orgName><p>This attribution was first added
                        during MLGB3 (2010-2015). A query was added to the attribution in 2026 when
                        Andrew G. Watson's Lewes attribution was incorporated into this record (see
                        below). MLGB3 recorded the following information in connection with the
                        Grimsby attribution:</p><p>
                        <q>Liber sermonum ex dono Reverendi in Christo dompni Joh. Danyell prioris
                           tali condicione ut ex eo usum habeat quamdiu vixerit</q> (fol. 7r).
                        According to an annotation in the Lambeth Palace Library copy of M. R.
                        James, in January 2001 James Carley identified Danyell as prior of the
                        Austin friars at Grimsby.</p></provenance>
                  <provenance type="#e" cert="low"><orgName role="fmo" key="org_310">Lewes, Sussex,
                        Cluniac priory of St Pancras</orgName><p>There is a Medieval Libraries of
                        Great Britain index card for this attribution, written by Andrew G. Watson
                        and crediting P. R. Robinson for the information. The card is dated 1993,
                        and therefore postdates the Medieval Libraries of Great Britain Supplement
                        (1987). The attribution appears to have been overlooked during MLGB3
                        (2010-2015). The card cites the same inscription as above (under Grimsby),
                        but instead identifies Danyell as prior of Lewes 1445-64, citing Emden,
                           <title>BRUC</title> 177.</p></provenance>
               </history>
